WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.402 --> 00:00:04.470
-President Trump held one of
his weirdest rallies yet

00:00:04.470 --> 00:00:05.638
as he tries to strip away

00:00:05.638 --> 00:00:07.540
the constitutional rights
of immigrants.

00:00:07.540 --> 00:00:09.609
For more on this,
it's time for "A Closer Look."

00:00:09.609 --> 00:00:14.848
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:14.848 --> 00:00:17.016
Trump last night
made another stop

00:00:17.016 --> 00:00:19.418
on his Orange Collar Comedy Tour

00:00:19.418 --> 00:00:22.221
where he held
a spectacularly unhinged rally

00:00:22.221 --> 00:00:23.356
in South Carolina.

00:00:23.356 --> 00:00:24.524
Now, these rallies
are very much

00:00:24.524 --> 00:00:26.592
like public therapy sessions
for Trump,

00:00:26.592 --> 00:00:29.095
but as things get worse for
Trump, politically and legally,

00:00:29.095 --> 00:00:30.930
these speeches
seem to get weirder.

00:00:30.930 --> 00:00:32.832
And last night was no exception,

00:00:32.832 --> 00:00:35.301
because he was
all over the place.

00:00:35.301 --> 00:00:37.303
-The Olympics
would've been a massive failure,

00:00:37.303 --> 00:00:39.939
and it turned out
to be a massive success.

00:00:39.939 --> 00:00:44.544
People did not want
to be nuked in a stadium.

00:00:44.544 --> 00:00:47.480
I said,
"Listen, you got rich guys,

00:00:47.480 --> 00:00:49.348
for whatever reason,
they love rockets."

00:00:49.348 --> 00:00:51.317
By the way,
I have the stupid teleprompters.

00:00:51.317 --> 00:00:53.286
You don't mind that I haven't
used them all night, do you?.

00:00:53.286 --> 00:00:55.888
"The Apprentice" --
Arnold Schwarzenegger,

00:00:55.888 --> 00:00:58.691
big movie star, took my place,
it bombed in about two shows.

00:00:58.691 --> 00:00:59.692
It was over.

00:00:59.692 --> 00:01:02.061
Mosquitos.
Lost many, many lives.

00:01:02.061 --> 00:01:04.563
They said she got a face lift.
No.

00:01:04.563 --> 00:01:08.134
If it's not your hair,
don't run for office, folks.

00:01:08.134 --> 00:01:09.802
We're not looking up in the air.

00:01:09.802 --> 00:01:12.138
Any rockets up there?
Any rockets?

00:01:12.138 --> 00:01:14.107
You know, they call them
the elites, right?

00:01:14.107 --> 00:01:15.908
"The elites."
You know what you are?

00:01:15.908 --> 00:01:18.277
You're the super elites.
I'm changing titles.

00:01:18.277 --> 00:01:21.114
-We are the super elites.

00:01:21.114 --> 00:01:23.482
[ Laughter ]

00:01:23.482 --> 00:01:26.886
-He is so dumb
he doesn't even understand

00:01:26.886 --> 00:01:29.922
that "elites"
was supposed to be an insult.

00:01:29.922 --> 00:01:32.224
"They called Democrats
out-of-touch intellectuals.

00:01:32.224 --> 00:01:35.194
Well, I say we're
further out-of-touch

00:01:35.194 --> 00:01:36.829
super intellectuals."

00:01:36.829 --> 00:01:38.063
[ Laughter ]

00:01:38.063 --> 00:01:40.066
Seriously, think about all
those random topics

00:01:40.066 --> 00:01:43.836
he just rambled on about
at an official campaign rally.

00:01:43.836 --> 00:01:45.137
Trump isn't the president.

00:01:45.137 --> 00:01:47.339
He's more like
one of those [bleep] algorithms

00:01:47.339 --> 00:01:50.209
that suggest other articles
you might want to read.

00:01:50.209 --> 00:01:51.644
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:01:51.644 --> 00:01:52.978
If you liked "build the wall,"

00:01:52.978 --> 00:01:54.447
you might also like
the Olympics,

00:01:54.447 --> 00:01:56.482
Arnold Schwarzenegger,
and rich guys love rockets.

00:01:56.482 --> 00:01:58.650
[ Laughter ]

00:01:58.650 --> 00:02:02.154
In fact,
on the topic of rockets --

00:02:02.154 --> 00:02:04.691
can't believe I'm saying that --
but on the topic of rockets,

00:02:04.691 --> 00:02:07.460
Trump, once again,
mumbled a few incoherent words

00:02:07.460 --> 00:02:09.628
about his proposal
to create a sixth branch

00:02:09.628 --> 00:02:11.731
of the military called
the Space Force.

00:02:11.731 --> 00:02:14.367
But this rant was somehow even
harder to follow

00:02:14.367 --> 00:02:16.035
than previous editions.

00:02:16.035 --> 00:02:19.505
-By the way,
NASA is now open for business.

00:02:19.505 --> 00:02:20.940
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:20.940 --> 00:02:23.609
You got all these guys sending
rockets all over the place.

00:02:23.609 --> 00:02:24.877
We'll get the credit.

00:02:24.877 --> 00:02:28.748
I said, "Lease them the land,
charge them a lot,

00:02:28.748 --> 00:02:30.850
but let's do it that way.
That's a lot better.

00:02:30.850 --> 00:02:32.151
We're like a landlord."

00:02:32.151 --> 00:02:35.154
You have all these rich guys.
I don't know what it is.

00:02:35.154 --> 00:02:37.823
They love rockets.

00:02:37.823 --> 00:02:39.525
I said, "This is great,
'cause, you know,

00:02:39.525 --> 00:02:42.628
you can't send rockets up, like,
down the street, right?

00:02:42.628 --> 00:02:46.832
You can't take the local plot,
the local Walmart,

00:02:46.832 --> 00:02:49.135
the local store,
and send a rocket.

00:02:49.135 --> 00:02:50.269
We're gonna win.

00:02:50.269 --> 00:02:52.638
Remember,
I said we're gonna win at trade,

00:02:52.638 --> 00:02:54.507
we're gonna win in space.

00:02:54.507 --> 00:02:56.642
-[ Laughing ]
The guy standing next to him's

00:02:56.642 --> 00:03:00.145
like, "Yeah,
we're gonna win at space."

00:03:00.145 --> 00:03:01.614
"We're gonna win at space,

00:03:01.614 --> 00:03:03.983
and we're gonna get
to board the spaceship first

00:03:03.983 --> 00:03:06.953
because we have
super-elite status."

00:03:06.953 --> 00:03:09.722
[ Laughter, cheers, applause ]

00:03:09.722 --> 00:03:11.190
But, of course...

00:03:11.190 --> 00:03:14.527
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:14.527 --> 00:03:16.396
...Trump cannot make it
through one rally

00:03:16.396 --> 00:03:18.363
without mentioning
the 2016 election.

00:03:18.363 --> 00:03:20.333
Now, there was a period of time
where it seemed like

00:03:20.333 --> 00:03:22.501
his obsession
was maybe waning a little bit.

00:03:22.501 --> 00:03:24.903
But last night,
it was like the good old days.

00:03:24.903 --> 00:03:28.107
All you had to do was
wind him up and watch him go.

00:03:28.107 --> 00:03:32.345
-You know, we won the state
of South Carolina by a lot.

00:03:32.345 --> 00:03:34.480
We had to run
the whole East Coast,

00:03:34.480 --> 00:03:38.117
and we got South Carolina,
and we got North Carolina.

00:03:38.117 --> 00:03:41.086
We got Pennsylvania,
and we got Florida.

00:03:41.086 --> 00:03:45.524
"Donald Trump has won
the state of Florida," right?

00:03:45.524 --> 00:03:49.495
They said, "North Carolina
is our firewall.

00:03:49.495 --> 00:03:51.730
South Carolina
we have no chance,

00:03:51.730 --> 00:03:53.399
but North Carolina..."

00:03:53.399 --> 00:03:56.803
And so we won South Carolina,
thank you very much.

00:03:56.803 --> 00:04:00.506
-Ugh! How many times are
you gonna tell this story?!

00:04:00.506 --> 00:04:06.446
[ Laughter, cheers, applause ]

00:04:06.446 --> 00:04:10.349
"Ugh!
Grandpa, I heard this story!"

00:04:10.349 --> 00:04:12.452
[ Laughter ]

00:04:12.452 --> 00:04:13.953
For Trump,
talking about the election

00:04:13.953 --> 00:04:15.955
is how he sooths his ego,
and, yesterday,

00:04:15.955 --> 00:04:17.856
he rambled on about it
for a very long time,

00:04:17.856 --> 00:04:19.425
at one point even acknowledging

00:04:19.425 --> 00:04:21.493
that he was
bragging about himself

00:04:21.493 --> 00:04:23.796
because no one else
would do it for him.

00:04:23.796 --> 00:04:28.434
-To win Wisconsin, which
hasn't been won in many years,

00:04:28.434 --> 00:04:30.169
like 1972, I think.

00:04:30.169 --> 00:04:31.470
That's a long time.

00:04:31.470 --> 00:04:35.941
To win Michigan, which hasn't
been won in a long time.

00:04:35.941 --> 00:04:38.610
You know, it's very interesting.
I just took this out.

00:04:38.610 --> 00:04:40.780
Sometimes you have
to toot your own horn,

00:04:40.780 --> 00:04:42.381
because nobody else
is gonna do it.

00:04:42.381 --> 00:04:43.983
Certainly,
they're not gonna do it.

00:04:43.983 --> 00:04:46.852
-Oh, you just figured that out?
[ Laughter ]

00:04:46.852 --> 00:04:49.188
You've been putting your name
on buildings for 40 years,

00:04:49.188 --> 00:04:52.258
and you just decided
it's time to toot your own horn?

00:04:52.258 --> 00:04:53.358
[ Laughter ]

00:04:53.358 --> 00:04:55.995
Also, you don't toot.

00:04:55.995 --> 00:04:58.597
You're constantly
blowing your horn.

00:04:58.597 --> 00:05:01.667
Your mouth is like a vuvuzela
at the World Cup.

00:05:01.667 --> 00:05:03.068
[ Laughter ]

00:05:03.068 --> 00:05:06.638
In facts your rallies would make
exactly the same amount of sense

00:05:06.638 --> 00:05:08.173
if they sounded like this.

00:05:08.173 --> 00:05:11.544
[ Vuvuzela blowing ]

00:05:11.544 --> 00:05:18.017
[ Laughter, cheers, applause ]

00:05:18.017 --> 00:05:20.352
But Trump's rambling
about the election

00:05:20.352 --> 00:05:22.287
somehow got weirder
because he insisted

00:05:22.287 --> 00:05:23.723
that a lot
of Hollywood celebrities

00:05:23.723 --> 00:05:25.925
voted for him
and decided to call out

00:05:25.925 --> 00:05:27.994
"Twin Peaks" creator
David Lynch.

00:05:27.994 --> 00:05:30.463
-Here's a story
that just came out.

00:05:30.463 --> 00:05:33.532
David Lynch --
you know, the great filmmaker.

00:05:33.532 --> 00:05:36.969
David Lynch -- he puts down --

00:05:36.969 --> 00:05:40.205
Headlines,
"Trump could go down --"

00:05:40.205 --> 00:05:42.141
This is a Hollywood guy.
The reason I do this is,

00:05:42.141 --> 00:05:46.012
you know, you don't hear this --
And plenty of them voted for me.

00:05:46.012 --> 00:05:47.880
Plenty of them voted for me.

00:05:47.880 --> 00:05:49.615
David Lynch --
"Could go down

00:05:49.615 --> 00:05:52.250
as one of the greatest
presidents in history."

00:05:52.250 --> 00:05:54.353
-I mean, it's weird,
but I guess it would make sense

00:05:54.353 --> 00:05:55.821
if David Lynch
liked Donald Trump.

00:05:55.821 --> 00:05:57.723
Donald Trump
is like the president

00:05:57.723 --> 00:06:01.494
from a dream sequence
in an episode of "Twin Peaks."

00:06:01.494 --> 00:06:03.128
[ Laughter ]

00:06:03.128 --> 00:06:09.035 line:0%
[ Speaking backwards ]

00:06:13.639 --> 00:06:15.641
[ Laughter ]

00:06:15.641 --> 00:06:17.543
Trump, of course,
also uses these rallies

00:06:17.543 --> 00:06:19.545
to rail against
his many perceived enemies,

00:06:19.545 --> 00:06:21.480
and one of those is
South Carolina Congressman

00:06:21.480 --> 00:06:23.082
Mark Sanford, a Republican

00:06:23.082 --> 00:06:24.783
who has sometimes
been critical of Trump.

00:06:24.783 --> 00:06:26.986
Now, you might remember
that, back in 2009,

00:06:26.986 --> 00:06:29.521
Sanford, as governor,
famously told his wife

00:06:29.521 --> 00:06:31.757
he was hiking
on the Appalachian Trail

00:06:31.757 --> 00:06:33.692
when, in fact,
he was having an affair,

00:06:33.692 --> 00:06:36.928
and Trump, who always remembers
your lowest moment,

00:06:36.928 --> 00:06:38.631
brought it up last night.

00:06:38.631 --> 00:06:41.333
Although he couldn't remember
the correct name

00:06:41.333 --> 00:06:43.235
for the Appalachian Trail.

00:06:43.235 --> 00:06:44.603
-Never liked him too much.

00:06:44.603 --> 00:06:45.871
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:45.871 --> 00:06:48.908
I wasn't a big fan.

00:06:48.908 --> 00:06:51.510
The Tallahassee Trail.
Must be a beautiful place.

00:06:51.510 --> 00:06:53.646
Unfortunately,
he didn't go there.

00:06:53.646 --> 00:06:56.849
-The Tallahassee Trail?

00:06:56.849 --> 00:06:58.751
That sounds like
the name of a strip club

00:06:58.751 --> 00:07:01.921
next to the Tallahassee airport.

00:07:01.921 --> 00:07:05.691
"Welcome to buffet night
at The Tallahassee Trail!

00:07:05.691 --> 00:07:08.394
Shrimp is all-you-can-eat,
and it is room temperature."

00:07:08.394 --> 00:07:09.695
[ Laughter ]

00:07:09.695 --> 00:07:11.863
Trump, of course, also remains
obsessed with the border

00:07:11.863 --> 00:07:14.166
and keeps lying about his
promise to build a wall there.

00:07:14.166 --> 00:07:17.235
In March, Congress allotted some
money for border security,

00:07:17.235 --> 00:07:19.872
but that money can be used only
to repair and build

00:07:19.872 --> 00:07:21.406
previously approved fencing.

00:07:21.406 --> 00:07:24.043
But when supporters broke out
into yet another chant

00:07:24.043 --> 00:07:26.945
to build that wall, Trump
continued to falsely insist

00:07:26.945 --> 00:07:29.281
that the wall
was already being built.

00:07:29.281 --> 00:07:32.684
-If you don't have borders,
you don't have a country.

00:07:32.684 --> 00:07:34.353
You don't have a country.

00:07:39.491 --> 00:07:41.293
Oh, it's happening.

00:07:41.293 --> 00:07:43.896
It's not
"build that wall" anymore.

00:07:43.896 --> 00:07:46.331
It's continue
building that wall.

00:07:46.331 --> 00:07:48.367
-"Continue building that wall."

00:07:48.367 --> 00:07:51.504
Not only is that wrong,
it's a much worse chant.

00:07:51.504 --> 00:07:53.505
[ Laughter ]

00:07:53.505 --> 00:07:54.740
Although I guess
it's better than

00:07:54.740 --> 00:07:56.609
"Continue building and repairing

00:07:56.609 --> 00:07:58.611
that previously approved
fencing!"

00:07:58.611 --> 00:08:00.112
[ Laughter ]

00:08:00.112 --> 00:08:04.083
Trump also continues to use
racist, dehumanizing language

00:08:04.083 --> 00:08:06.051
to talk about immigrants,
and now he's calling

00:08:06.051 --> 00:08:08.921
for stripping them of their
constitutionally protected

00:08:08.921 --> 00:08:11.057
due-process rights
and deporting them

00:08:11.057 --> 00:08:14.126
without being able to make
their case in front of a judge.

00:08:14.126 --> 00:08:17.196
-We want very tight,
very strict borders.

00:08:17.196 --> 00:08:20.499
And they came to me
three days ago.

00:08:20.499 --> 00:08:22.535
"Sir, we'd like you
to sign this order."

00:08:22.535 --> 00:08:23.669
What is the order?

00:08:23.669 --> 00:08:27.640
"We need 5,000 judges
on the border."

00:08:27.640 --> 00:08:30.709
I said, "Judges?
What other country has judges?"

00:08:30.709 --> 00:08:36.481
I said, "Where are you gonna
find 5,000 people to be judges?

00:08:36.481 --> 00:08:37.916
How many do we have now?"

00:08:37.916 --> 00:08:39.184
"I don't know the number."

00:08:39.184 --> 00:08:40.186
They don't even know the number

00:08:40.186 --> 00:08:41.587
even though
they're in charge, okay?

00:08:41.587 --> 00:08:44.857
-No, dude, you're in charge.

00:08:44.857 --> 00:08:46.058
[ Laughter ]

00:08:46.058 --> 00:08:48.226
That's the deal.

00:08:48.226 --> 00:08:49.695
That's like if your pilot
got on the PA and said,

00:08:49.695 --> 00:08:54.533
"Okay, folks, I asked the tower
what airport we're going to,

00:08:54.533 --> 00:08:56.802
and they said they don't know,
and I certainly don't, either."

00:08:56.802 --> 00:08:58.070
[ Laughter ]

00:08:58.070 --> 00:09:00.906
"So, sit back and relax,
and a special welcome aboard

00:09:00.906 --> 00:09:03.442
to all our super-elite members.

00:09:03.442 --> 00:09:05.110
[ Laughter ]

00:09:05.110 --> 00:09:08.414
Also, can we go back to this
for just a second.

00:09:08.414 --> 00:09:12.184
-We need
5,000 judges on the border.

00:09:12.184 --> 00:09:15.420
I said, "Judges?
What other country has judges?"

00:09:15.420 --> 00:09:18.424
-What other country has judges?

00:09:18.424 --> 00:09:21.560
Lots of --
Most other countries.

00:09:21.560 --> 00:09:24.063
In the Netherlands,
they even have judges

00:09:24.063 --> 00:09:25.998
at a special court in the Hague,

00:09:25.998 --> 00:09:28.334
and who knows -- maybe
you'll get to meet them one day.

00:09:28.334 --> 00:09:30.936
You don't --
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:09:30.936 --> 00:09:34.373
You don't know, but you might.

00:09:34.373 --> 00:09:36.975
But Trump hasn't
always felt so cavalier

00:09:36.975 --> 00:09:38.644
about
the due-process protections

00:09:38.644 --> 00:09:40.145
provided by the Constitution.

00:09:40.145 --> 00:09:42.614
He's trying to strip them away
from immigrants now,

00:09:42.614 --> 00:09:44.517
but when his own staffers
are being investigated

00:09:44.517 --> 00:09:45.985
as part of
the Russian investigation,

00:09:45.985 --> 00:09:49.088
he felt very differently about
the importance of due process.

00:10:03.802 --> 00:10:04.937
So, Trump wants to strip away

00:10:04.937 --> 00:10:06.572
the constitutional rights
of immigrants,

00:10:06.572 --> 00:10:08.340
but when it's his own aides
being investigated,

00:10:08.340 --> 00:10:10.509
he suddenly sounds like a guy
being dragged away

00:10:10.509 --> 00:10:13.178
from the buffet for trying
to put shrimp in his pockets.

00:10:13.178 --> 00:10:14.412
"How dare you!

00:10:14.412 --> 00:10:16.282
There's such thing any longer
as due process!

00:10:16.282 --> 00:10:18.751
I'm never coming back
to The Tallahassee Trail!"

00:10:18.751 --> 00:10:20.318
[ Laughter ]

00:10:20.318 --> 00:10:22.021
Trump and the GOP
only care about

00:10:22.021 --> 00:10:24.489
seizing political power and
using it to restrict the rights

00:10:24.489 --> 00:10:25.658
of marginalized pe ople.

00:10:25.658 --> 00:10:27.526
Just take Trump's Muslim ban,
which was upheld

00:10:27.526 --> 00:10:29.996
by the Supreme Court today
in a 5-4 ruling

00:10:29.996 --> 00:10:32.998
after Republicans installed
Justice Neil Gorsuch at a seat

00:10:32.998 --> 00:10:34.967
that should've been filled
by President Obama.

00:10:34.967 --> 00:10:38.036
The various versions of the ban
were so sloppy and ill-conceived

00:10:38.036 --> 00:10:40.506
that even Trump officials,
like former White House

00:10:40.506 --> 00:10:42.308
press secretary, Sean Spicer,

00:10:42.308 --> 00:10:44.109
couldn't keep
their stories straight

00:10:44.109 --> 00:10:45.878
on whether or not it was a ban.

00:10:49.615 --> 00:10:51.283
-Well, first of all,
it's not a travel ban.

00:10:51.283 --> 00:10:52.618
It's a 90-day ban.

00:10:52.618 --> 00:10:54.620
I think a million people
have now come into this country.

00:10:54.620 --> 00:10:55.988
That's not a ban.

00:10:55.988 --> 00:10:57.823
The ban deals
with seven countries.

00:10:57.823 --> 00:11:00.759
It can't be a ban if you're
letting a million people in.

00:11:00.759 --> 00:11:02.661
-The President himself
called it a ban.

00:11:02.661 --> 00:11:03.729
-I understand.

00:11:03.729 --> 00:11:05.063
-Is he confused,
or are you confused?

00:11:05.063 --> 00:11:06.064
-No, I'm not confused.

00:11:06.064 --> 00:11:07.666
-Yeah, you are.

00:11:07.666 --> 00:11:10.002
Sean Spicer
always answered questions

00:11:10.002 --> 00:11:11.804
like a dude passed out
in the bushes

00:11:11.804 --> 00:11:14.306
after a concert in Central Park.

00:11:14.306 --> 00:11:15.941
"Sir, is that
a vape in your hand?"

00:11:15.941 --> 00:11:17.543
"Uh, yeah, it's a vape.

00:11:17.543 --> 00:11:21.480
No, I mean,
it's an inhaler, uh, for weed."

00:11:21.480 --> 00:11:23.416
